# 22. Relation to Future RV64GC Support

The processor is already parameterized using "XLEN".

Current configuration:

XLEN = 32

The privileged architecture should therefore avoid unnecessarily hard-coding 32-bit assumptions.

A future RV64GC implementation would require the CSR and privileged architecture to support:

XLEN = 64

This would affect CSR widths and other architectural state.

However, RV64GC is not the goal of this project.

The purpose here is to create a clean privileged-architecture foundation that can later be extended if RV64GC becomes part of the project.

